
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('aaac9647-2064-4974-b970-c95c02e861bd', 'Alice''s Adventures in Wonderland', 'Join little Alice as she gently tumbles down a magical rabbit hole into a world filled with whimsical creatures and enchanting adventures. In this dreamy land, she meets curious characters, learns valuable lessons, and discovers the beauty of imagination. As the sun sets, Alice finds her way home, ready to drift into a peaceful sleep, filled with dreams of wonder and joy.', 'The moral of the story is: Embrace your curiosity and the joy of new adventures, for they can lead you to wonderful friendships and help you discover who you are. Always remember that your imagination can take you to magical places!', 'Once upon a time, in a cozy little village, there lived a sweet girl named Alice. One sunny afternoon, while she sat by a gentle stream, she spotted a fluffy white rabbit wearing a tiny waistcoat. The rabbit looked quite hurried, glancing at his watch and saying, "Oh dear! Oh dear! I shall be late!" Curiosity sparkled in Alice''s eyes, and she decided to follow him.

As she chased the rabbit through a lovely garden, Alice suddenly found herself tumbling down a soft, velvety rabbit hole. Down, down, down she went, landing softly in a wonderland filled with shimmering colors and delightful sounds. The air was filled with the sweet scent of flowers, and the trees danced gently in the breeze.

Alice looked around in wonder. "Hello!" she called out, and to her surprise, a friendly little mouse appeared. "Welcome to Wonderland!" he said with a smile. "Would you like to join us for a tea party?"

Delighted, Alice followed the mouse to a beautiful table set under a giant mushroom. There, she met a cheerful March Hare and a sleepy Dormouse. They poured warm tea into tiny cups and shared the most delicious treats. They laughed and chatted, and Alice felt so happy surrounded by her new friends.

After the tea party, Alice wandered further into Wonderland. She met a curious Caterpillar who sat on a mushroom, puffing on a little hookah. "Who are you?" he asked in a soft, dreamy voice. Alice thought for a moment and replied, "I’m not quite sure, but I’m finding out!" The Caterpillar nodded wisely, and Alice felt a sense of understanding wash over her.

As she continued her journey, Alice came across a garden filled with vibrant flowers that danced in the sunlight. They sang sweet melodies, and Alice joined in their joyful song. She twirled and spun, feeling light as a feather and full of bliss.

Soon, she met a lovely Cheshire Cat who appeared and disappeared with a smile. "If you don’t know where you want to go, then it doesn’t matter which way you go," he said, comforting Alice with his gentle wisdom.

Feeling a little sleepy from her adventures, Alice decided it was time to find her way back home. As she wandered through the enchanting land, she heard the soft whispers of the trees and the gentle rustle of the leaves, guiding her back to the rabbit hole.

Finally, Alice reached the place where she had first fallen into Wonderland. With a warm smile, she thanked all her friends for the wonderful adventures they had shared. As she climbed back up the rabbit hole, she felt the cozy embrace of her home waiting for her.

As Alice settled into her bed, she closed her eyes and remembered the magical creatures and beautiful places she had seen. The stars twinkled outside her window, and she drifted off to sleep, dreaming of whimsical wonders and the joy of imagination.

And so, in her sweet dreams, Alice knew that Wonderland would always be a part of her heart, waiting to welcome her back whenever she wished. 

Goodnight, dear Alice. Sweet dreams await.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516979187457-637abb4f9353?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'adapted from Lewis Carroll', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('648735a1-6de0-4a59-8f33-729ca812ee1c', 'Through the Looking-Glass', 'Join Alice as she steps through a magical mirror into a whimsical world filled with friendly characters and delightful adventures. In this enchanting land, she meets peculiar creatures and learns important lessons about kindness and imagination. As the day comes to a close, Alice finds her way back home, carrying the joy of her adventures in her heart, ready for sweet dreams.', 'The magic of friendship and imagination can take you on wonderful adventures, even when you least expect it. Always carry the joy and magic in your heart, and remember that every day is a chance for a new adventure!', 'Once upon a time, in a cozy little house, a curious girl named Alice found a magical mirror. One day, while gazing at her reflection, she noticed that the mirror shimmered and sparkled as if inviting her in. With a gentle smile, Alice stepped through the glass and into a wondrous world on the other side.

In this enchanting land, everything was turned upside down! The trees grew in strange shapes, and the skies were painted in soft pastel colors. Alice giggled as she walked along a path made of fluffy clouds. Suddenly, she spotted a friendly Red Queen sitting on a throne of soft pillows.

"Welcome, dear Alice!" the Red Queen said with a warm smile. "Here, we play games and share stories. Would you like to join us?"

Alice''s eyes sparkled with excitement. "Oh, yes, please!" she exclaimed. The Red Queen led her to a meadow where playful creatures danced and sang. There were fluffy rabbits, cheerful birds, and even a wise old turtle who told the most delightful tales.

As the sun began to set, painting the sky with shades of lavender and gold, Alice felt a sense of joy in her heart. She played games of tag with the rabbits and listened to the turtle''s stories that lulled her into a peaceful state. With every laugh and every adventure, she felt a little more at home in this magical land.

After a while, Alice noticed that the Red Queen had grown quiet, watching the day fade into a soft twilight. "Alice," she said gently, "every adventure must come to an end, but remember, you can always carry the magic with you in your heart."

Alice nodded, understanding that it was time to return. She thanked the Red Queen and all her new friends for the wonderful day. As she walked back to the mirror, she felt a warm glow of happiness. Each step reminded her of the laughter and joy she had shared.

When Alice stepped back through the mirror, she found herself in her cozy room, snuggled under her soft blanket. The stars twinkled outside her window, whispering sweet dreams to her.

With a contented sigh, Alice closed her eyes, thinking of the wonderful friends she had made and the adventures they had shared. She drifted off to sleep, carrying the magic of the mirror world in her heart, ready to dream of all the delightful possibilities that awaited her.

And so, dear little one, as you snuggle in bed tonight, remember that adventures can happen in the most unexpected places, and the magic of dreams is always just a wish away. Goodnight, sleep tight!', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1604004555489-723a93d6ce74?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'adapted from Lewis Carroll', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('443f2c52-3103-4ab4-9c04-7c3aa9d6aad2', 'The Wonderful Wizard of Oz', 'Join little Dorothy as she embarks on a magical journey to the enchanting land of Oz. Along the way, she meets new friends, including a kind Scarecrow, a brave Tin Man, and a courageous Lion. Together, they seek the wise Wizard of Oz, learning the importance of friendship and believing in oneself. This heartwarming tale ends with Dorothy finding her way home, surrounded by love and warmth.', 'The greatest treasures in life are love and friendship. Always believe in yourself and help others, just like Dorothy and her friends did on their adventure!', 'Once upon a time, in a little house on the Kansas prairie, there lived a sweet girl named Dorothy. She had a little dog named Toto, who was her very best friend. One day, a strong wind swept through the land, lifting Dorothy and Toto into the sky and carrying them far away to a magical place called Oz.

When Dorothy landed softly on the golden road of Oz, she looked around in wonder. Everything was bright and colorful, and beautiful flowers danced in the gentle breeze. Dorothy felt a little scared but also very excited. She wanted to find her way back home, so she decided to follow the yellow brick road, which she heard led to the wonderful Wizard of Oz.

As she walked along the road, Dorothy soon met a Scarecrow who was stuck on a pole. He looked very sad, and Dorothy asked him why. "I wish I had a brain so I could think and talk like everyone else," he said with a sigh. Dorothy smiled and said, "You can come with me to see the Wizard. I’m sure he can help you!" The Scarecrow was thrilled, and together they continued down the yellow brick road.

Further along, they came upon a Tin Man who was rusted and unable to move. "Oh dear!" Dorothy exclaimed. "What’s wrong?" The Tin Man replied, "I long for a heart so I can love and feel like everyone else." Dorothy’s heart was full of kindness, and she said, "Join us! The Wizard can help you too!" The Tin Man smiled, and with a little help, he was soon free and ready to join their adventure.

As they traveled together, they heard a soft roar in the distance. It was a Lion, who looked fierce but was actually quite timid. "I wish I had courage," he said with a shaky voice. Dorothy gently said, "Come with us to see the Wizard. I believe you are braver than you think!" The Lion felt a spark of hope and joined the merry group.

Now with her three new friends — the Scarecrow, the Tin Man, and the Lion — Dorothy felt much braver. They journeyed through beautiful fields, sparkling rivers, and magical forests. Along the way, they shared stories, laughter, and kindness, and Dorothy realized how important friendship was on this adventure.

Finally, they reached the grand City of Emeralds, where the Wizard of Oz lived. With hearts full of hope, they entered the magnificent palace. The Wizard was a great and powerful figure who listened to their wishes. He told the Scarecrow that he already had a brain filled with clever thoughts, the Tin Man that love was already in his heart, and the Lion that courage was within him all along.

As for Dorothy, the Wizard revealed a special secret: she had the power to go home all along. With a few taps of her red shoes, she could return to her home in Kansas. Dorothy felt a warm glow of love and gratitude for her friends and the lessons she had learned.

With a tender goodbye to the Scarecrow, Tin Man, and Lion, Dorothy tapped her shoes together and said, "There’s no place like home!" In an instant, she found herself back in her cozy little house with Toto wagging his tail joyfully.

As night fell over Kansas, Dorothy snuggled under her blankets, her heart full of love. She knew that she would always carry her friends and the magic of Oz within her. With a sweet smile, she closed her eyes, drifting off to dreamland, where adventures awaited her in the land of dreams. Goodnight, dear child, and remember, love and friendship are the greatest treasures of all.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1476234251651-f353c1b3e3a1?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'adapted from L. Frank Baum', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('b101453e-7acf-47dd-ac12-4181619aadd0', 'Peter Pan', 'Join Peter Pan, the boy who never grows up, as he takes Wendy, John, and Michael on magical adventures in the enchanting land of Neverland. Together, they meet fairies, pirates, and playful lost boys. As the stars twinkle above, they learn the importance of dreams, friendship, and the joy of returning home. A soothing tale that invites sweet dreams and peaceful slumber.', 'The magic of friendship makes every adventure special, and even when our journeys end, the memories we share can always stay in our hearts. Remember to dream big and cherish the moments with those you love!', 'Once upon a time, in a cozy little home in London, lived a boy named Peter Pan. He was not just any boy; he was a special boy who could fly and never grew up. One night, while exploring the children''s bedroom, Peter met Wendy, John, and their little brother Michael. He invited them to fly away with him to a magical place called Neverland.

With a sprinkle of fairy dust from Tinker Bell, Peter and the children soared into the night sky, laughing with delight as they flew above the twinkling stars. They left the world behind and soon arrived in Neverland, where the trees whispered secrets and the flowers danced in the gentle breeze.

In Neverland, they met the Lost Boys, a cheerful group of friends who lived in a cozy treehouse and loved to play. Together, they had wonderful adventures, exploring the shimmering lagoons and lush green meadows. They played games, shared stories, and laughed until their bellies hurt. Wendy loved to tell them tales of faraway places, and the Lost Boys listened with wide eyes, enchanted by her words.

But Neverland was also home to the mischievous Captain Hook, a pirate who wanted to capture Peter Pan. One day, as the sun began to set and the sky turned shades of pink and purple, Captain Hook and his pirates appeared! Peter and the Lost Boys bravely stood together, ready to protect their home. With clever tricks and a sprinkle of courage, they outsmarted the pirates, sending them sailing away on their ship.

After the excitement, they gathered around a soft, glowing campfire. The stars twinkled brightly above them, and the gentle sounds of the night filled the air. Wendy looked at her brothers and the Lost Boys, feeling grateful for the fun they had shared. She whispered, "This is the best adventure ever!"

As the moonlight danced on the water, Peter Pan turned to his friends and said, "Every adventure must come to an end, but our dreams can always continue. You can visit me in your dreams whenever you wish!" The children nodded, knowing that although they would return home, they would always carry the magic of Neverland in their hearts.

As the night grew deeper, Peter Pan led Wendy, John, and Michael back to their cozy home in London. With one last sprinkle of fairy dust, they floated down softly to their bedroom, where the familiar warmth of their blankets welcomed them. Peter smiled and said, "Remember, you can always find me among the stars. Goodnight, dear friends. Sweet dreams!"

With that, Peter Pan waved goodbye and flew back to Neverland, where adventures awaited him still. The children snuggled into their beds, closing their eyes, filled with dreams of flying, fairy dust, and endless adventures. And as they drifted off to sleep, the gentle night whispered, "Goodnight, little dreamers, goodnight."', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516571748831-5d81767b788d?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'adapted from J. M. Barrie', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('32cf5837-42ae-4de0-ac9b-d502b3f8e4e5', 'The Wind in the Willows', 'Join Mole, Ratty, and the spirited Toad as they explore the beauty of the riverbank in this gentle tale of friendship and adventure. Along their journey, they discover the joys of nature, the comforts of home, and the importance of being true to oneself. As the sun sets, they find peace and warmth in each other''s company, ready for sweet dreams.', 'True friendship means having fun together and always looking out for one another. It''s important to be safe while we explore and enjoy our adventures!', 'Once upon a time, in a peaceful little riverbank, there lived a kind-hearted Mole who had just woken up from a long winter''s nap. As he peeked out from his cozy burrow, he felt the warm sun on his face and heard the soft whispers of the breeze. Excited for the day, Mole decided to explore the world beyond his home.

As he waddled along, Mole soon met a gentle Water Rat, known as Ratty, who was busy preparing a delightful picnic by the river. "Come and join me!" called Ratty with a cheerful smile. Mole''s eyes sparkled with joy as he accepted the invitation. They shared a lovely meal of fresh bread and sweet berries, laughing and telling stories as the river sparkled in the sunlight.

"Let’s go on an adventure!" suggested Ratty. So, hand in hand, they set off along the riverbank, watching the dragonflies dance and the ducks paddle by. They splashed in the cool water and picked colorful flowers, reveling in the beauty of the day.

As they wandered, they came across a charming little house, where the whimsical Toad lived. Toad was a very spirited character, always dreaming of grand adventures. He welcomed his friends with open arms, his eyes shining with excitement. "Let’s take a ride in my shiny new motorcar!" he exclaimed.

Mole and Ratty were a little worried, but Toad''s enthusiasm was infectious. They climbed into the car, and off they went, zooming down the road. The wind rushed through their fur, and they laughed with delight! But soon, Toad got carried away, and the car went a little too fast. They had a little bump, and the adventure turned into a gentle lesson.

After the excitement, they returned to Toad''s house where he realized that friendship and safety were more important than speed. "I’m sorry, my friends! I promise to be more careful," Toad said with a warm smile. Mole and Ratty nodded, happy to have their adventurous friend by their side.

As the sun began to set, painting the sky in soft hues of orange and pink, the three friends settled down by the riverbank. They shared their dreams and stories, feeling grateful for the joy of friendship. The gentle sound of the water flowing nearby lulled them into a peaceful state.

Mole sighed contentedly, “What a wonderful day we’ve had!” Ratty nodded, his eyes growing heavy. Toad, too, felt the weariness of the day wash over him. They nestled together under the twinkling stars, surrounded by the soothing sounds of nature.

And as they drifted off to sleep, they knew that tomorrow would bring more adventures, laughter, and the warmth of friendship. With their hearts full of joy and minds at ease, they closed their eyes, dreaming sweet dreams by the riverbank, where the wind whispered softly through the willows. 

Goodnight, dear friends, and may your dreams be as wonderful as the adventures of Mole, Ratty, and Toad.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709594023-6eab9bab7b23?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'adapted from Kenneth Grahame', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('203a8d58-9c3d-4b91-b15a-e15625318775', 'The Velveteen Rabbit', 'In a cozy nursery, a soft velveteen rabbit dreams of becoming real through the love of a little boy. As they share adventures, the rabbit learns that true love can make even the simplest things special. Join the velveteen rabbit on a heartwarming journey that teaches the magic of love and friendship, perfect for a peaceful bedtime story.', 'Love is what makes us special and real, just like the velveteen rabbit. Remember, when we care for each other, our hearts become full of magic and joy.', 'Once upon a time, in a bright and cheerful nursery, there lived a soft velveteen rabbit. He had beautiful, velvety fur and shiny button eyes that sparkled in the sunlight. But there was one thing the rabbit longed for more than anything else in the world: to be real. 

The velveteen rabbit was not alone. He had a special friend, a little boy who loved him dearly. Each night, the boy would cuddle the rabbit close, whispering sweet dreams as they drifted off to sleep together. The rabbit felt warm and happy in the boy''s arms, but still, he wondered what it meant to be real. 

One day, as the boy played with his toys, he noticed how much he loved the rabbit. He would take him on exciting adventures around the nursery, making up stories about brave bunnies and magical lands. As the days passed, the rabbit felt the boy''s love wrapping around him like a cozy blanket. 

One sunny morning, the boy took the rabbit outside into the garden. There, they explored the colorful flowers and listened to the birds singing sweet melodies. The rabbit was filled with joy! He felt more alive than ever, surrounded by the beauty of nature and the warmth of the boy''s laughter. 

But one day, the boy fell ill and had to stay in bed. The little rabbit sat close by, keeping him company. The boy''s mother noticed how much the rabbit meant to her son and decided to wash him to make him fresh and clean. 

When the rabbit was taken away, he felt sad. He missed the boy''s hugs and the cozy nursery. But he also knew that the boy loved him, and that love was a powerful thing. As he was washed, he felt the warmth of the boy''s love shining through him. 

Days passed, and the boy got better. When he saw his beloved rabbit again, he hugged him tightly, and the rabbit felt something wonderful happen. The boy''s love had made him real! He was no longer just a toy; he had grown special and alive in the boy''s heart. 

From that day forward, the velveteen rabbit and the boy shared countless adventures, exploring the garden, playing games, and dreaming sweet dreams together. The rabbit learned that love is what makes us truly special and real. 

As night fell, the stars twinkled in the sky, and the nursery became quiet and peaceful. The velveteen rabbit snuggled into the boy''s arms, feeling safe and loved. And as they drifted off to sleep, the rabbit knew that no matter what happened, he would always be real in the boy''s heart. 

And so, the velveteen rabbit and the little boy slept soundly, surrounded by love, dreaming of all the wonderful adventures waiting for them in the morning light. 

Goodnight, little one. May you always feel the magic of love, just like the velveteen rabbit.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516979187457-637abb4f9353?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'adapted from Margery Williams', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('b2cbf63f-bb36-4fca-b2c0-2e163b4945b1', 'A Christmas Carol', 'In a cozy, snowy town, there lived a grumpy old man named Scrooge. One magical Christmas Eve, he met three friendly spirits who showed him the joy of kindness, love, and giving. As Scrooge learned about the warmth of Christmas, he discovered the happiness that comes from caring for others. Join us on this heartwarming journey of transformation and joy.', 'The true magic of Christmas comes from sharing love and kindness with others. Remember, it''s never too late to change and make the world a better place!', 'Once upon a time, in a chilly little town, there lived a grumpy old man named Ebenezer Scrooge. Scrooge was known for his cold heart and his love for counting coins instead of sharing smiles. He didn’t believe in Christmas or the magic it brought. His days were spent in solitude, grumbling at those who celebrated the season with joy.

One chilly Christmas Eve, as snowflakes danced outside his window, Scrooge returned home after a long day. He was startled when he saw a shadowy figure appear in his room. It was the ghost of his old friend, Jacob Marley, who had come to warn him.

“Ebenezer,” Marley said softly, his voice like a gentle breeze, “I wear the chains I forged in life, and they clink and clank to remind me of my greed. You still have the chance to change. Tonight, you will be visited by three spirits. Listen to them.” With that, Marley vanished into thin air.

Scrooge was puzzled but soon fell asleep. Just as the clock chimed one, a warm light filled his room, and the first spirit appeared. This was the Ghost of Christmas Past, a gentle figure that shimmered like starlight.

“Come with me, Scrooge,” said the spirit, and with a flutter, they were whisked away to scenes from Scrooge’s own past. They visited his childhood school, where he saw himself as a lonely little boy, longing for love and friendship. Then, they watched as he celebrated joyful moments with friends and family, laughter echoing in the air. Scrooge felt a warmth in his heart as he remembered the happiness of those days.

Next, the Ghost of Christmas Present arrived, beaming with joy and surrounded by a feast of delicious food. “Look around, Scrooge!” the spirit exclaimed. They visited the homes of those who celebrated Christmas with love, even those who had little to share. Scrooge saw his humble clerk, Bob Cratchit, who was filled with cheer, despite having very little. He witnessed Bob’s family, especially Tiny Tim, who was small but had a big heart, spreading happiness to everyone around him.

“God bless us, everyone!” Tiny Tim said with a sweet smile, and Scrooge felt a tug at his heart. He realized how important it was to care for one another, no matter how little they had.

Finally, the last spirit arrived: the Ghost of Christmas Yet to Come. This ghost was quiet and mysterious, showing Scrooge a future that was dark and lonely. Scrooge saw a world where no one cared, where he was forgotten, and where Tiny Tim was not there to brighten the day. Scrooge felt sadness wash over him.

“Please, spirit! I can change! I don’t want this to be my future!” he cried out, his heart full of hope.

With a start, Scrooge woke up in his own bed, sunlight streaming through the window. It was Christmas Day! Joy bubbled in his chest as he realized he had a chance to make things right.

He rushed to the window and called out to a passing boy, “You there! What day is it?”

“It’s Christmas Day, sir!” the boy replied with a grin.

Scrooge laughed with delight, filled with the spirit of Christmas. He hurried out into the streets, greeting everyone with warmth and kindness. He bought a giant turkey for the Cratchit family and delivered it with joy. He shared in their laughter and celebrated with them, making sure Tiny Tim had the best Christmas ever.

From that day on, Scrooge became known as a kind and generous man, filling the hearts of everyone around him with love and cheer. He learned that Christmas was not just a day, but a spirit of giving and caring.

And so, on that peaceful Christmas night, as the stars twinkled in the sky, Scrooge fell asleep with a smile, knowing he had found his heart and the true magic of the season. 

And everyone lived happily ever after, wrapped in the warmth of love and kindness. Goodnight.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1604004555489-723a93d6ce74?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'adapted from Charles Dickens', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('6fe4f19d-39a5-4566-96f5-0c47db8aebc0', 'The Secret Garden', 'In a quiet, hidden corner of the world, a lonely girl named Mary discovers a magical garden that has long been forgotten. As she nurtures the blossoms and befriends the creatures within, Mary learns the beauty of friendship and the joy of helping things grow. Together, they create a place of happiness and wonder, reminding us all of the magic that lies in nature and love.', 'The secret garden teaches us that with love and care, we can help ourselves and others grow stronger and happier. When we nurture friendships and take responsibility for the world around us, we create a beautiful place where joy can bloom. Remember, a little kindness can make a big difference!', 'Once upon a time, in a faraway land, there lived a little girl named Mary Lennox. Mary was not like most children; she was often sad and lonely, having spent her early years in a distant country. But one day, everything changed.

Mary was sent to live with her uncle, Mr. Craven, in a grand and mysterious mansion. The house was large and filled with whispers of the past, but Mary felt very much alone. The gardens outside were overgrown, and the flowers seemed to have forgotten how to bloom. Mary often wandered the halls, feeling as if she were a ghost in a forgotten world.

One day, while exploring the mansion, Mary heard a soft, rustling sound coming from a hidden door. Curious, she pushed it open and stumbled into a secret garden! The air smelled sweet, and the sunbeams danced gently upon the ground. But the garden was wild and untended, its flowers hiding shyly among the tangled vines.

Mary felt a spark of excitement in her heart. She decided that she would take care of this enchanting place. Every day, she visited the garden, pulling weeds, watering the plants, and singing to the flowers. Slowly but surely, the garden began to awaken. Bright colors emerged, and the once-sleepy blooms stretched their petals towards the sky.

As Mary worked in the garden, she met a kind boy named Dickon. He had a special way with animals and nature, and they quickly became friends. Together, they nurtured the garden, filling it with laughter and joy. The little creatures of the garden—birds, rabbits, and even a friendly fox—joined in their fun, creating a symphony of cheerful sounds.

Mary also discovered that her uncle had a son named Colin, who was very sick and had never seen the outside world. With Dickon''s encouragement, Mary invited Colin to the garden. At first, Colin was frightened, but Mary and Dickon gently coaxed him to join them.

As Colin stepped into the sunlight, a magical transformation began. With every day spent in the garden, Colin grew stronger and bolder. He laughed and played with Mary and Dickon, and soon he was able to walk and run among the flowers. The garden had worked its wonders, bringing joy and health to all who entered.

As spring blossomed into summer, the secret garden became a place of happiness and friendship. The children learned about the beauty of nature and the importance of caring for living things. They understood that love and kindness could help anything grow, whether it was a flower or a friendship.

One peaceful evening, as the sun began to set, Mary, Dickon, and Colin sat together in the garden, surrounded by the fragrant flowers. The sky turned shades of pink and orange, and they felt a warm glow in their hearts. They knew that they had created something truly special—a place where dreams could bloom.

As the stars twinkled above, Mary whispered softly, "This garden is our secret, a place of love and magic. We will always come back here to remember the joy we found together." And with that, they closed their eyes, feeling the gentle breeze, knowing that their hearts were forever tied to the beauty of the secret garden. 

And so, under the watchful gaze of the moon, the three friends drifted into a peaceful sleep, dreaming of flowers, laughter, and the endless wonders that awaited them in their magical garden.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1476234251651-f353c1b3e3a1?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'adapted from Frances Hodgson Burnett', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('07a5c1bb-79e4-4bd8-ac14-ef3c2f57144b', 'Little Women', 'In a cozy little house, four sisters—Meg, Jo, Beth, and Amy—navigate life, love, and dreams during a time of great change. As they face challenges and celebrate joys together, their bond grows stronger. This heartwarming tale reminds us of the importance of family, kindness, and cherishing each moment, leading to a peaceful end where love and dreams illuminate their hearts.', 'The story of the March sisters teaches us that love and kindness are the greatest gifts we can share with others. By putting our family first and supporting each other, we can overcome challenges and make beautiful memories together. Remember, no matter how different we may be, our love for one another makes us strong.', 'Once upon a time, in a cozy little house nestled in a quiet town, lived four sisters—Meg, Jo, Beth, and Amy March. They were kind-hearted girls full of dreams and laughter, living during a time when the world was changing all around them.

Meg, the oldest, had a gentle spirit and loved to take care of her sisters. She dreamed of having a beautiful home and a loving family. Jo, with her wild hair and adventurous heart, was a storyteller who loved writing tales of bravery and friendship. Sweet Beth, shy and tender, had a special gift for playing the piano, filling their home with soft, soothing melodies. And little Amy, the youngest, was an artist with a heart full of color, always dreaming of grand adventures and beautiful things.

Though times were tough because of the Civil War, the sisters found joy in each other. They played games, shared secrets, and often helped their mother, Marmee, with chores around the house. Every evening, they would gather by the warm fire, sharing stories of their day and dreaming of their futures.

One chilly winter evening, the girls decided to use their meager savings to buy gifts for their mother instead of for themselves. They wanted to show her how much they loved and appreciated her. Each sister picked something special—Meg chose a lovely pair of gloves, Jo found a beautiful book, Beth picked a lovely handkerchief, and Amy chose a small bottle of perfume.

On Christmas morning, their eyes sparkled with excitement as they presented their gifts to Marmee. She was so touched by their love and generosity that her heart swelled with pride. They spent the day together, laughing and creating joyful memories, each sister feeling the warmth of love within their hearts.

As the seasons passed, the sisters faced challenges, but they always leaned on each other for support. Jo’s adventurous spirit sometimes clashed with Meg’s desire for a more traditional life. They learned to appreciate their differences and found strength in their love for one another. Beth continued to play beautiful music, which brought comfort to everyone around her, and little Amy grew into a talented artist, painting the world with her dreams.

One summer evening, as the sun began to set, the sisters gathered outside under a sky filled with twinkling stars. They shared their dreams, hopes, and aspirations. Jo spoke of writing a book, Meg dreamed of a family, Beth wished for her music to bring joy to others, and Amy wanted to travel the world.

As the stars began to shimmer brighter, their hearts filled with warmth, they promised to always be there for one another, no matter where life took them. They knew that together, they could overcome anything.

As the night grew deeper, the sisters returned to their cozy home, their hearts full of love and dreams. They snuggled under their blankets, whispering sweet goodnights and sharing soft giggles until their eyes grew heavy with sleep. In the gentle embrace of their family, they drifted off, knowing that their bond was unbreakable and their dreams would always guide them.

And so, the four sisters slept peacefully, surrounded by love, laughter, and the promise of tomorrow.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516571748831-5d81767b788d?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'adapted from Louisa May Alcott', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('5251810d-e1d3-49a3-85f7-d2947f17a442', 'The Jungle Book', 'In a lush jungle of India, a little boy named Mowgli is found and raised by a loving family of wolves. As he grows, he learns the ways of the jungle, befriends many animals, and discovers the importance of kindness and courage. Join Mowgli on his gentle adventures, where friendship and love light the path to a peaceful bedtime.', 'Always be brave and kind, for love and understanding can bring harmony to even the fiercest of hearts. Together, we can create a happy world where everyone belongs.', 'Once upon a time, in a vast and beautiful jungle in India, there was a little boy named Mowgli. One day, while wandering through the trees, he got lost. But soon, he was found by a friendly family of wolves who decided to take him in. They welcomed him with open paws and gave him a warm, loving home.

Mowgli learned the language of the jungle and played with his wolf brothers and sisters. They taught him how to run fast, climb trees, and listen to the gentle whispers of the wind. Mowgli felt safe and happy, surrounded by his furry family.

Every day was filled with new adventures. Mowgli met Baloo, a wise and gentle bear who loved to share stories and teach him about the fruits of the jungle. Baloo would often say, "Life is sweet, like honey, my dear Mowgli!" And Mowgli would giggle as he helped Baloo find the ripest fruits.

One day, Mowgli came across a clever panther named Bagheera. Bagheera was sleek and graceful, always watching over Mowgli with loving eyes. He taught Mowgli the importance of being brave and respectful to all creatures in the jungle. "You must listen to your heart, little one," Bagheera would say, "for it will guide you home."

But not all the animals in the jungle were friendly. There was a fierce tiger named Shere Khan, who wanted to chase away anyone who dared to enter his territory. Mowgli knew he had to be brave, but he also understood that kindness was the key to peace.

One sunny afternoon, while playing near the river, Mowgli saw Shere Khan lurking in the shadows. Instead of running away, Mowgli took a deep breath and approached the tiger with a gentle heart. "Hello, Shere Khan," he said softly. "I believe we can find a way to share this jungle together."

Shere Khan was surprised by Mowgli''s courage. The little boy''s kindness melted the tiger''s fierce heart. "Perhaps you are not so bad after all, little one," he grumbled. Mowgli smiled, knowing that even the fiercest creatures could learn to be gentle.

As the days turned into weeks, Mowgli continued to grow and learn from his friends. He discovered the beauty of friendship and the joy of understanding one another. The jungle became a harmonious place, where every animal, big and small, learned to live together in peace.

One evening, as the sun dipped below the trees and painted the sky with soft pinks and oranges, Mowgli sat with his wolf family, Baloo, and Bagheera by the riverbank. The sounds of the jungle sang a soothing lullaby, and Mowgli felt a warm glow in his heart.

"I am grateful for my family and friends," he whispered, looking at the twinkling stars above. "We share this beautiful jungle, and together, we are happy."

As the stars began to twinkle, Mowgli closed his eyes, dreaming of new adventures and the loving jungle that surrounded him. The gentle breeze wrapped around him like a soft blanket, and soon, he drifted off to sleep, knowing that love and kindness would always guide his way.

And so, in the heart of the jungle, Mowgli''s gentle spirit continued to shine, bringing peace and harmony to all. Goodnight, dear Mowgli, and goodnight to all the creatures of the jungle. May your dreams be filled with sweet adventures and love.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709594023-6eab9bab7b23?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'adapted from Rudyard Kipling', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('8261fdaf-0721-4be9-86e0-c37698d2ef8a', 'Cinderella', 'Once upon a time, in a cozy little home, there lived a kind girl named Cinderella. Though she had a challenging life, her heart was filled with love and kindness. With the help of her magical fairy godmother, she was able to attend a splendid ball, where dreams come true and happiness blooms. Join Cinderella on her gentle journey to find joy and love, as she learns that kindness is the greatest magic of all.', 'The moral of the story is: "Kindness and believing in yourself can bring magic into your life. Always stay hopeful, and your dreams can come true!"', 'Once upon a time, in a quiet little village, there lived a kind girl named Cinderella. She lived with her stepmother and two stepsisters, who often treated her unkindly. Despite the challenges she faced, Cinderella remained gentle and sweet, always finding joy in the little things around her, like the blooming flowers and the starry nights.

One sparkling evening, the royal palace announced a grand ball. Everyone in the village was excited, especially Cinderella’s stepsisters, who spent hours preparing their beautiful dresses. Cinderella longed to go to the ball, but her stepmother told her she couldn’t attend, as she had too many chores to do.

As Cinderella sat by the fireplace, feeling a little sad, something magical happened. With a twinkle of light and a soft, soothing voice, her fairy godmother appeared. "Dear Cinderella," she said, "do not worry. I am here to help you. You shall go to the ball!"

With a wave of her wand, the fairy godmother transformed Cinderella’s simple dress into a beautiful gown that sparkled like the stars. She even turned a pumpkin into a lovely carriage and mice into fine horses. "But remember, my dear, you must return before the clock strikes midnight," the fairy godmother warned.

Cinderella’s heart filled with joy as she thanked her fairy godmother and stepped into the carriage. As she arrived at the ball, everyone was captivated by her beauty and grace. The prince, with his kind smile, took her hand and led her to dance. They twirled and spun, their laughter echoing like music through the grand hall.

As the evening continued, Cinderella felt like she was in a dream. She shared sweet conversations and joyful dances with the prince, forgetting all her worries. But as the clock began to chime, Cinderella remembered her fairy godmother''s warning. She hurriedly said goodbye to the prince and rushed out of the palace.

In her haste, one of her lovely glass slippers slipped off her foot. The prince, seeing the slipper, picked it up with a gentle smile, determined to find the girl who had stolen his heart.

The next day, the prince searched the kingdom, carrying the delicate slipper. When he arrived at Cinderella’s home, her stepsisters tried on the slipper, but it was too small for them. With a hopeful heart, Cinderella stepped forward and tried on the slipper. To everyone’s surprise, it fit perfectly!

The prince’s eyes lit up with joy as he recognized Cinderella from the ball. He took her hand, and together they returned to the palace, where they celebrated with laughter and kindness. Cinderella’s heart was filled with happiness, and she knew she had found a friend in the prince.

As they spent time together, Cinderella and the prince shared stories, laughter, and dreams. They quickly understood that kindness and love were the greatest treasures of all. And so, they lived happily ever after, surrounded by love and laughter.

As the stars twinkled in the night sky, Cinderella smiled, knowing that dreams really do come true when you believe in the magic of kindness. And with that beautiful thought, she drifted off to sleep, dreaming of wonderful adventures to come.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516979187457-637abb4f9353?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'adapted from Charles Perrault', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('4fd1162f-b14a-4c5e-a735-234d1feb81f7', 'Sleeping Beauty', 'Once upon a time, in a faraway kingdom, a lovely princess named Aurora was blessed and cursed by a mysterious fairy. As she grew, she faced a magical slumber that would last a hundred years. But true love and a gentle kiss would awaken her. Join us as we journey through the enchanted forest to discover the power of love and dreams.', 'In a world filled with kindness and love, true friendship can bring joy and happiness, even in the toughest times. Always believe in the magic of love and the beauty of your dreams!', 'In a beautiful kingdom, where flowers bloomed and birds sang sweet melodies, there lived a lovely princess named Aurora. She had golden hair that shimmered like the sun and a smile that could light up the darkest days. The people of the kingdom adored her, and on the day of her birth, a grand celebration took place.

The king and queen invited all the fairies from far and wide to bless their precious daughter. Each fairy brought a special gift of love and joy. One fairy bestowed the gift of beauty, another gave the gift of kindness, and a third fairy shared the gift of laughter. But, oh dear, there was one fairy who had not been invited to the celebration, and she was very unhappy.

In a swirl of magic and sparkles, the angry fairy appeared before the guests. "Since I have not been invited, I shall cast a spell upon the princess!" she declared. With a wave of her wand, she proclaimed, "On her sixteenth birthday, Aurora shall prick her finger on the sharp spindle of a spinning wheel and fall into a deep sleep for one hundred years!"

The king and queen were filled with sorrow, but one gentle fairy, who had not yet shared her gift, stepped forward. "Do not fear, dear ones," she said softly. "While Aurora will indeed fall into a slumber, my gift is that she shall be awakened by a true love''s kiss."

As the years passed, Aurora grew into a kind and gentle young woman, filled with dreams and laughter. Though her parents tried their best to keep her safe, on the eve of her sixteenth birthday, she discovered an old spinning wheel hidden away in a forgotten room. Curious as a little bird, she reached out to touch it, and in that moment, she pricked her finger.

Suddenly, the magic of the curse took hold. Aurora''s eyes fluttered, and she gently fell into a deep, peaceful sleep. The entire kingdom fell silent, as if holding its breath. Flowers began to grow around the castle, and vines wrapped themselves gently around the walls, creating a beautiful and serene garden.

Many years went by, and the tale of the sleeping princess spread across the lands. Young princes from all over came to the castle, hoping to awaken Aurora with their love. But their kisses could not break the spell, and they left, hearts heavy with longing.

Then, one day, a kind-hearted prince named Henry heard the story of the princess. He was brave and gentle, and he felt a warm glow in his heart when he thought of Aurora. Determined to save her, he journeyed to the enchanted castle, where he found the lovely princess resting amidst the flowers.

As he approached, he felt a soft breeze, and he knelt beside her. With tenderness, he brushed a gentle kiss on her forehead, whispering, "Sleep sweetly, dear Aurora. I am here."

In that moment, the magic of true love awoke in the air. Aurora slowly opened her eyes, and the kingdom blossomed back to life with joy and laughter. The birds sang, and the flowers danced in the sunlight.

Aurora smiled at Prince Henry, her heart filled with warmth. "Thank you for waking me, kind prince," she said softly. They spent their days exploring the enchanting garden and sharing stories under the stars.

As the sun set, painting the sky in hues of pink and gold, Aurora and Henry knew that their love would always bring happiness and dreams. And so, they lived together in peace, surrounded by love, as they drifted off to sleep, knowing that their dreams would be filled with magic and adventure forever more. 

Goodnight, dear children. May your dreams be as sweet as Aurora’s, filled with love and wonder.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1604004555489-723a93d6ce74?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'adapted from Charles Perrault', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('0d0bb644-35a8-4a43-b25c-5f820d6c8de1', 'Little Red Riding Hood', 'In a serene forest, a sweet girl named Little Red Riding Hood embarks on a lovely journey to visit her grandmother. Along the way, she meets a curious wolf who shares a gentle conversation with her. This delightful tale teaches us about kindness, bravery, and the importance of listening to our hearts, all while creating a warm and peaceful atmosphere perfect for bedtime.', 'Always be kind and friendly, because you can find wonderful friendships in the most surprising places!', 'Once upon a time, in a cozy little village surrounded by a peaceful forest, there lived a kind-hearted girl known to everyone as Little Red Riding Hood. She was named for the lovely red cloak her grandmother had made for her, which she wore every day.

One bright morning, Little Red Riding Hood''s mother asked her to take a basket of goodies to her grandmother''s house, which was on the other side of the gentle woods. "Remember, dear," her mother said softly, "to stay on the path and not to talk to strangers."

With a cheerful smile and a wave goodbye, Little Red Riding Hood set off on her adventure. The sun shone through the leaves, creating a beautiful dance of light and shadows on the forest floor. The birds chirped sweet melodies, and the flowers swayed gently in the breeze.

As she walked along the path, Little Red Riding Hood noticed a friendly wolf sitting under a tree. He had soft, fluffy fur and bright, curious eyes. "Hello there!" the wolf said kindly. "Where are you going on this lovely day?"

Little Red Riding Hood smiled back. "Hello! I’m going to visit my grandmother. She lives in a cozy cottage at the other end of the forest. I have a basket of treats for her!"

The wolf’s eyes sparkled with interest. "That sounds delightful! But why don’t you pick some flowers for your grandmother along the way?" he suggested, pointing to a patch of colorful blossoms nearby. 

Little Red Riding Hood thought this was a wonderful idea. "Thank you for the suggestion!" she replied. She wandered off the path for a moment to gather some beautiful flowers. As she filled her basket with blooms, she felt a warm sense of happiness.

Meanwhile, the clever wolf had a thought. He wanted to surprise Little Red Riding Hood''s grandmother! So, he dashed ahead through the forest, taking a shortcut to reach the grandmother''s house first. When he arrived, the grandmother welcomed him with a smile.

"What a lovely visitor!" she said. The wolf quickly explained that he was a friend of Little Red Riding Hood and asked if he could take her place for a moment. The grandmother, being a kind soul, agreed, thinking it would be a fun game.

The wolf then snuggled up in the grandmother''s bed, pulling the covers up to his chin, and waited for Little Red Riding Hood to arrive.

Not long after, Little Red Riding Hood finished picking flowers and continued on her way. When she reached her grandmother’s house, she knocked gently on the door. "Grandmother, it’s me, Little Red Riding Hood!" she called.

"Come in, dear!" said the wolf, trying to sound like the grandmother. Little Red Riding Hood opened the door and walked inside. She noticed something was different. "Oh, Grandmother! You look a little different today."

The wolf smiled, his eyes twinkling. "I’m just feeling a little under the weather, my dear. Come closer so I can see you better!"

As Little Red Riding Hood stepped closer, she suddenly recognized the wolf! "Oh, dear! You’re not my grandmother!" she exclaimed, but she was not afraid. Instead, she remembered the wolf’s kind words and realized he was just curious.

With a gentle laugh, Little Red Riding Hood said, "Oh, you silly wolf! You shouldn’t trick people, even for fun. Let’s be friends instead!" The wolf’s ears perked up with joy at her kindness.

From that day on, Little Red Riding Hood and the wolf became the best of friends. They shared stories, laughter, and even visited her grandmother together. Little Red Riding Hood learned that sometimes, understanding and friendship can bloom in the most unexpected places.

As the sun began to set, casting a soft golden glow over the forest, Little Red Riding Hood and the wolf walked home together, enjoying the gentle sounds of nature. They waved goodbye, knowing they would meet again soon. And as Little Red Riding Hood lay down to sleep that night, she smiled, dreaming of her adventures in the forest, filled with kindness and friendship.

And so, dear little one, as you close your eyes tonight, remember that friendship can be found in the most surprising places, and kindness makes the world a brighter place. Sweet dreams await you!', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1476234251651-f353c1b3e3a1?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'adapted from Charles Perrault', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('dc2d3fb8-78f4-42c2-ac18-9cd876dae1f0', 'Bluebeard', 'In a quaint little village, a kind and curious woman named Lily discovers a hidden secret in her loving husband, Mr. Blue. As she explores the mysterious rooms of their charming home, she learns the importance of trust and understanding. Join Lily on her adventure, where curiosity leads to valuable lessons and a peaceful resolution, perfect for a bedtime tale.', 'The moral of the story is: "It''s important to respect each other''s feelings and secrets, but sharing our thoughts can make our love even stronger. When we understand and support each other, we can face anything together."', 'Once upon a time in a lovely village, there lived a kind woman named Lily. She was married to a man named Mr. Blue, who had a charming home filled with laughter and joy. Mr. Blue was a gentle husband, always caring and attentive to Lily''s needs. However, he held a small secret that he had never shared with anyone.

One sunny afternoon, as the golden sun streamed through their cozy home, Lily noticed a mysterious door that had always been locked. Curious as she was, she couldn''t help but wonder what lay behind it. Mr. Blue had told her many stories about their home, but he had never mentioned this door. 

Lily''s heart was filled with curiosity, and she decided to ask Mr. Blue about it. "Darling, what lies behind that locked door?" she gently inquired.

Mr. Blue smiled softly, his eyes twinkling like stars. "My dear Lily, that room is my private space, where I keep my thoughts and memories. It’s best left undisturbed, for it holds things that are very special to me."

Though she understood his words, Lily’s curiosity grew stronger. She promised herself to respect his wishes, but the door called to her imagination. Each day, she would glance at it, wondering what hidden treasures it contained. 

One evening, while Mr. Blue was busy preparing a lovely dinner, Lily could no longer resist. She tiptoed toward the locked door, her heart fluttering with excitement and nervousness. With a gentle twist of the handle, she found that it opened slightly, just enough for her to peek inside. 

As she entered, she gasped softly at the sight before her. The room was filled with beautiful memories—pictures of Mr. Blue’s past, lovely trinkets, and stories of adventures he had taken before they met. But in the corner of the room, she found something that made her heart sink—a collection of items that seemed to tell a sad story. 

Realizing that these were reminders of Mr. Blue’s struggles and the hard times he had faced, Lily felt a wave of compassion wash over her. She understood now that Mr. Blue had kept this part of his life private not because he wanted to hide it, but because he wished to protect her from sadness. 

Lily gently closed the door and returned to the kitchen, where the delicious aroma of dinner filled the air. When Mr. Blue finished cooking, they sat down together to eat. As they shared their meal, Lily felt a warmth in her heart, knowing that understanding and love were the most important treasures of all.

After dinner, Lily took Mr. Blue''s hands in hers and said softly, "I found your special room, and I understand now why you kept it a secret. Thank you for sharing your life with me, even the difficult parts. I love you, and I want to support you through everything."

Mr. Blue''s eyes sparkled with gratitude. He smiled and replied, "Thank you, dear Lily. It means the world to me that you understand. Let’s always share our hearts with each other."

From that day on, their bond grew stronger. Lily learned the value of trust and compassion, while Mr. Blue felt safe sharing his past. Together, they created new memories, filled with love and understanding. And so, as the moon rose high in the night sky, casting a gentle glow over their home, they drifted off to sleep, wrapped in each other’s warmth, knowing that they could face anything together. 

And they all lived happily ever after, dreaming sweet dreams beneath the stars.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516571748831-5d81767b788d?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'adapted from Charles Perrault', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('c473f28a-bafd-42b4-897c-96acd9edc042', 'Puss in Boots', 'In a quaint little village, a kind-hearted young man inherits a clever cat named Puss. With the help of Puss''s quick thinking and clever tricks, they embark on a delightful adventure to bring happiness and fortune to their lives. Together, they discover the magic of friendship and the importance of believing in one another, ending their journey with sweet dreams and contentment.', 'True friendship can help us achieve great things, and being clever and brave can change our lives for the better. Always believe in yourself and your friends!', 'Once upon a time, in a cozy little village, there lived a kind young man named Jack. Jack was gentle and loved by everyone, but he had little more than a few simple belongings. One day, he inherited a lovely cat from his father. This wasn’t just any cat; this was a clever cat named Puss.

As Jack looked at Puss, he noticed the glimmer of intelligence in the cat''s bright eyes. ''What shall we do now, dear Puss?'' Jack asked, feeling a bit lost. Puss, with a soft purr, replied, ''Fear not, my dear friend! I shall help you find fortune, and together we will live happily ever after.'' 

With a swish of his tail, Puss sprang into action. He asked Jack to give him a pair of fine boots and a little bag. Jack was curious but trusted his clever cat. Once Puss was dressed in his lovely boots, he set off to find a way to make Jack rich.

Puss traveled to the grand palace of the king, where he encountered the royal guards. With a charming smile, he introduced himself as the faithful servant of the noble Lord of Carabas. ''My master is quite wealthy,'' he said with a twinkle in his eye, ''and he would be honored to meet the king.'' 

The guards were curious, so they allowed Puss to proceed. Soon enough, Puss found the king and told him wonderful tales about the greatness of Lord Carabas. The king, intrigued, invited Jack to the palace. The clever cat had woven a tale of wealth that would impress anyone.

When Jack arrived at the palace, he was surprised to see the grand hallway filled with golden decorations. Puss had made Jack look like a nobleman! The king welcomed him warmly, and as they chatted, Puss made sure to keep everyone entertained with his charming antics.

But Puss had another clever plan! He dashed back to the river where a great ogre lived. This ogre was known for his strength and magic. Puss approached the ogre with bravery and said, ''I hear you can transform into any creature you wish. Is it true?'' The ogre, flattered, agreed to show off his talents. He transformed into a mighty lion, roaring proudly.

Puss, quick as a wink, said, ''I bet you cannot change into something smaller, like a mouse.'' The ogre, eager to impress, turned into a tiny mouse. And just like that, Puss pounced and caught the mouse in a flash!

Returning to the palace with the ogre''s fate cleverly sealed, Puss told the king of the ogre''s defeat. The king was so impressed with Jack''s bravery and Puss''s cleverness that he offered Jack a place in his court and a beautiful home of his own.

Jack was overjoyed! With Puss by his side, he found happiness and success. They became the best of friends, sharing laughter and adventures every day. 

As the stars twinkled in the night sky, Jack and Puss cuddled together in their cozy home. ''Thank you, dear Puss,'' Jack whispered, feeling grateful for his clever cat. ''You’ve changed my life.'' 

Puss purred softly, ''And you’ve brought me a wonderful friend. Together, we will dream of more adventures to come.'' 

With hearts full of joy and dreams of tomorrow, Jack and Puss drifted off to sleep, enveloped in warmth and love, ready to embrace whatever magic the next day would bring. And so, they lived happily ever after, in a world where friendship was the greatest treasure of all.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709594023-6eab9bab7b23?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'adapted from Charles Perrault', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('94d3a027-8b1e-48c1-9532-73256d637865', 'Beauty and the Beast', 'In a quaint village, a kind-hearted girl named Belle discovers that true beauty lies within. When her father is captured by a mysterious Beast, she bravely offers to take his place. As Belle spends time with the Beast, she learns about friendship, love, and the importance of looking beyond appearances. This enchanting tale reminds us that kindness and understanding can transform the world around us.', 'Always look for the kindness in others, for true beauty comes from the heart. Love and friendship can change everything.', 'Once upon a time, in a charming little village, there lived a sweet and gentle girl named Belle. She loved reading books and dreaming about adventures far away. Belle had a loving father who built little trinkets and toys, and they lived happily together.

One day, while wandering through the woods, Belle’s father got lost and stumbled upon a grand, mysterious castle. Inside, he was captured by a fierce Beast who lived there. The Beast, though gruff and intimidating, was lonely and misunderstood. He had once been a handsome prince, cursed to remain in this form until someone could see the beauty within him.

When Belle learned that her father was in trouble, she bravely decided to take his place. "Let him go, and take me instead!" she said, her voice steady but gentle. The Beast agreed, and Belle entered the castle, feeling a mix of fear and curiosity.

At first, the castle seemed dark and cold, and the Beast frightened her. But as days turned into weeks, Belle discovered that the Beast had a kind heart beneath his fearsome exterior. He showed her the beautiful gardens and the library filled with books—her favorite place of all. The more time they spent together, the more she saw his gentle spirit, hidden behind his rough appearance.

One evening, as they shared a simple meal, Belle noticed the sadness in the Beast''s eyes. "Why are you so sad?" she asked softly. The Beast sighed and shared his story, and Belle listened with empathy. She realized that he was not just a scary creature, but a friend who needed love and understanding.

As Belle and the Beast grew closer, they shared laughter and stories, and Belle found herself caring for him deeply. One day, while walking in the garden, Belle noticed a single rose blooming brightly among the thorns. It reminded her of the Beast—how something so beautiful could grow in such an unexpected place.

One night, Belle had a dream of a handsome prince who whispered to her, "Look with your heart, and you will see true beauty." When she woke up, Belle felt a warmth in her heart. She realized that she had fallen in love with the Beast, not for his looks, but for his kind soul.

But one fateful day, Belle received news that her father was unwell. The Beast, seeing her worry, gently encouraged her to go home. "You must care for your father," he said softly, his voice filled with love. Belle promised to return, and the Beast’s heart ached as she left.

Days passed, and Belle’s father recovered, but Belle missed the Beast dearly. She returned to the castle, and to her surprise, she found the Beast heartbroken and alone. As she rushed to him, she declared, "I love you, dear Beast!" At that moment, a warm light surrounded them, and the Beast transformed back into a handsome prince.

Belle gasped in amazement, but she smiled, for she knew that the true magic was in love and kindness. The prince, now free from the curse, thanked Belle for seeing beyond his appearance. They embraced, knowing that they would always cherish each other’s hearts.

From that day forward, Belle and the prince lived happily in the castle, sharing stories, laughter, and love. The villagers soon learned of their tale, and they visited often, bringing joy and friendship. 

As the stars twinkled in the night sky, Belle and the prince would sit by the window, whispering sweet dreams to one another. And in the gentle glow of the moonlight, they knew that love could indeed change everything.

And so, under the peaceful night, they drifted off to sleep, their hearts forever intertwined, dreaming of adventures yet to come. 

Goodnight, dear one. Remember, true beauty shines from within.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516979187457-637abb4f9353?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'adapted from Jeanne-Marie Leprince de Beaumont', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('819c3ecc-99d7-40e8-9628-566b5a587b8f', 'Hansel and Gretel', 'In a cozy forest, two brave siblings named Hansel and Gretel embark on a gentle adventure. When they find a delightful gingerbread house, their curiosity leads them to discover its secrets. Together, they learn about kindness and courage, ultimately finding their way back home, where love and warmth await them. This tale reminds us that together, we can face any challenge and return to the safety of our dreams.', 'Always remember that love and bravery can help you find your way home, no matter how lost you feel. Together with friends and family, you can face any adventure!', 'Once upon a time, in a little village nestled by a whispering forest, there lived two dear siblings named Hansel and Gretel. They were the best of friends, always exploring and laughing together. One sunny day, they wandered into the forest, chasing butterflies and picking wildflowers. But as the sun began to set, they realized they had strayed far from home.

“Oh dear!” said Hansel, looking around at the tall trees that seemed to stretch up to the sky. “We are lost!”

Gretel held his hand tightly, but she smiled. “Let’s be brave, Hansel. We can find our way back together!” With a little courage in their hearts, they ventured deeper into the woods.

As twilight painted the sky with soft shades of pink and purple, the siblings stumbled upon a most enchanting sight—a house made entirely of gingerbread! Its walls were frosted with sweet icing, and candy adorned the roof like a sparkling crown. Hansel’s eyes widened with delight. “Oh, Gretel, look! It’s a magical house!”

The aroma of sweet treats filled the air, inviting them closer. They couldn’t resist taking a small bite of the candy door. “It’s delicious!” Gretel giggled, her worries melting away like the sugary sweets.

But as they munched happily, a gentle voice called from inside the house. “Come in, dear children! There’s plenty to share!”

Curious and a bit cautious, Hansel and Gretel stepped inside. The room was warm and cozy, filled with the scent of freshly baked cookies. An old woman with kind eyes greeted them. “Welcome, little ones! I’ve been waiting for you!”

At first, the children felt safe and happy, enjoying the treats and stories the old woman shared. But as the night grew darker, they began to notice something strange. The woman’s eyes sparkled with mischief, and her smile, though warm, felt a little too wide. 

“Perhaps it’s time for bed,” she suggested, her voice soft yet commanding. Hansel and Gretel exchanged worried glances. They remembered their cozy home and the loving embrace of their parents. Together, they whispered, “We want to go home.”

The old woman’s face changed, and for a moment, they felt fear creep into their hearts. But then, Gretel took a deep breath and spoke gently. “We appreciate your kindness, but we must return to our family. Love is more important than sweets.”

Hearing her brave words, the old woman’s expression softened. “You are wise beyond your years, dear Gretel. Love is indeed the sweetest treat of all. I will help you find your way home.”

With a wave of her hand, the trees outside shimmered in the moonlight, revealing a path that sparkled with stardust. “Follow this path, and it will lead you back to your village.”

Thankful and relieved, Hansel and Gretel hugged the old woman tightly, their hearts filled with gratitude. “Thank you for your kindness,” they said as they stepped onto the shimmering path.

As they walked, the forest seemed to whisper secrets of the night, guiding them safely home. Soon, they could see the warm glow of their cottage in the distance. Their hearts danced with joy as they ran into their loving parents’ arms.

That night, as they snuggled into their cozy beds, Hansel and Gretel shared stories of their adventure, feeling grateful for the love that surrounded them. They drifted off to sleep, dreaming of magical worlds, knowing that together, they could face anything. And in their dreams, the sweet scent of gingerbread danced softly in the air, a reminder of their brave hearts and the warmth of home. 

And so, dear little listener, remember that love and bravery always lead us back to where we belong. Goodnight.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1604004555489-723a93d6ce74?w=800&h=600&fit=crop', 'en', false, 'en', 'adapted from Jacob & Wilhelm Grimm', NULL, true, 0);
INSERT INTO stories (id, title, summary, moral, full_content, image_url, language, is_translated, original_language, author_name, author_id, is_public, like_count) VALUES ('bfd47490-284f-4d59-910a-13a1bc87461e', 'Snow White', 'In a land far away, a kind princess named Snow White finds safety and friendship with seven cheerful dwarfs. As she hides from her unkind stepmother, Snow White learns the importance of love and friendship. Together, they create a warm, happy home filled with laughter and joy, leading to a peaceful and magical ending for all.', 'The moral of the story is: True friends will always stand by you, and kindness and love can overcome even the toughest challenges. Always be careful of what you trust, and remember that goodness shines brighter than jealousy.', 'Once upon a time, in a beautiful kingdom, there lived a sweet princess named Snow White. She had skin as white as snow, lips as red as a rose, and hair as black as ebony. Snow White lived with her stepmother, the queen, who was very vain and always wanted to be the fairest of them all. Every day, she would ask her magic mirror, "Mirror, mirror on the wall, who is the fairest of them all?" And every day, the mirror would reply, "You, my queen, are fair; it''s true. But the young princess is a thousand times more beautiful than you." This made the queen very angry and jealous.

One day, the queen summoned a huntsman and ordered him to take Snow White deep into the forest and never return with her. But the kind huntsman couldn''t bear to harm the gentle princess. Instead, he told Snow White to run far away and never look back, promising to keep her secret safe. 

Snow White ran and ran until she was very tired. Eventually, she came upon a little cottage hidden among the trees. She gently pushed the door open and peeked inside. The cottage was cozy and warm, filled with tiny furniture and lovely little decorations. She felt so at home that she decided to rest for a while.

After a short nap, Snow White woke up to the sound of cheerful voices. To her surprise, seven little dwarfs came home from their day of work in the mines. They were amazed to find the sweet princess in their home. Snow White smiled at them, and they welcomed her with open arms, happy to have a friend.

The dwarfs were named Doc, Grumpy, Happy, Sleepy, Bashful, Sneezy, and Dopey. They all agreed that Snow White could stay with them, and they promised to protect her from the wicked queen. Together, they spent their days singing, dancing, and playing in the forest. Snow White loved to cook and clean for her new friends, and the dwarfs loved to keep her company.

However, the wicked queen soon discovered that Snow White was still alive. In her anger, she decided to disguise herself as an old peddler woman and visit the cottage. She brought with her a lovely, shiny apple, offering it to Snow White. "Just one bite will make you feel so happy, dear princess," she said with a wicked smile.

Snow White, being kind and trusting, took a bite of the apple. But as soon as she did, she felt very sleepy and fell into a deep slumber. The dwarfs returned home just in time to find their dear friend lying still on the floor. They were heartbroken and placed her gently in a glass coffin, hoping that one day she would awaken.

Days turned into weeks, and the dwarfs stayed by her side, keeping watch and sharing stories of adventures they had together. One day, a kind prince happened upon the cottage. He had heard tales of the beautiful princess and felt a warmth in his heart when he saw her. He leaned down and kissed Snow White softly on her cheek.

As if awakened by true love’s kiss, Snow White opened her eyes and smiled at the prince. The dwarfs cheered with joy, and Snow White was filled with happiness. She thanked the prince, and they decided to celebrate together with her dear friends.

From that day on, Snow White and the prince returned to the castle, and the queen, realizing she could never be the fairest again, vanished into the forest. Snow White lived happily ever after with the prince and her seven dear friends, where love and laughter filled their days.

